    "created_at": "2018-09-06T23:22:26Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-09-06T23:22:26Z",
    "body": "It... prevents the browser from being slow.  In particular, it prevents *the rest* of the browser from janking because you're doing some updates in *one particular* subtree that doesn't *need* to immediately update its layout/rendering.\r\n\r\nThis is just a slightly more explicit (and thus predictable) way of telling the browser \"updating the layout/rendering of this subtree is low priority\".",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
